    "q-107606": {
      "dom_id": "step-q107606",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "What is the volume of a rectangular solid that has length, width, and height of $2\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m},$ $4\\,\\text{m},$ and $3\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m},$ respectively?",
      "worked_solution": "We can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=2\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m},\\,w=4\\,\\text{m},\\,h=3\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nV=2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3}=24\\sqrt{6}\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
