    "q-107620": {
      "dom_id": "step-q107620",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224606/assets/abec41d02ba71b2e94d7b2c3cd92f552ddab907de494719a22706b568a588be4.png)\n\nDetermine the length of the rectangular solid above given that its volume is $84\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nV=84,\\,w=3\\sqrt{2},\\,h=\\sqrt{8}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain the following\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}84 & =l\\cdot 3\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{8} \\\\ 84 & =3\\sqrt{16}l \\\\ 84 & =12l \\\\ l & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length is $7\\,\\text{cm}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
